<article class="env-lemma" id="04KY">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04KY">Lemma <span data-tag="04KY">33.8.14</span>.</a> Let $k$ be a field, with separable algebraic closure $\overline{k}$. Let $X$ be a scheme over $k$. The fibres of the map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \text{IrredComp}(X_{\overline{k}}) \longrightarrow \text{IrredComp}(X)  \]
</div>
  <p> of Lemma <a href="/tag/04KX" data-tag="04KX">33.8.11</a> are exactly the orbits of $\text{Gal}(\overline{k}/k)$ under the action of Lemma <a href="/tag/038J" data-tag="038J">33.8.13</a>. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $T \subset X$ be an irreducible component of $X$. Let $\eta \in T$ be its generic point. By Lemmas <a href="/tag/04KW" data-tag="04KW">33.8.10</a> and <a href="/tag/04KX" data-tag="04KX">33.8.11</a> the generic points of irreducible components of $\overline{T}$ which map into $T$ map to $\eta $. By Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/04KP" data-tag="04KP">10.47.14</a> the Galois group acts transitively on all of the points of $X_{\overline{k}}$ mapping to $\eta $. Hence the lemma follows. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>